 {"id": "DF-BOARDCTL-47", "title": "[P2] umbrella aborts the WHOLE cross-board view on one unparseable line in one child board (no --skip-bad-lines) — every other verb has a degrade mode", "status": "complete", "priority": "P2", "reasoning": "Dogfood run 25, HEAD 900b7b5. Umbrella view over the real fleet pair boardctl (187 tasks) + warpfs (411 tasks): the census printed the boardctl line, then died on warpfs's line 412 duplicate `worker_status` key with `boardctl: board warpfs (/home/kara/warpfs/.coding-hermes/board): ... line 412: duplicate key \"worker_status\" in row`, rc=1 — no per-repo stats, no grand total, no list, nothing. `umbrella --skip-bad-lines` → `boardctl: flag provided but not defined: -skip-bad-lines`; umbrella --help documents no degrade mode at all, while validate, render and normalize-board all ship `--skip-bad-lines` and prior runs had to add normalize-board for the same second-dialect class (DF-BOARDCTL-36). Impact: the one surface whose purpose is a fleet-wide answer returns nothing for the fleet whenever ANY child board carries a single bad line — a routine live condition (warpfs's line appeared mid-day today), and the reading user is told nothing about the other boards' health.", "created_at": "2026-10-23T11:23:17Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-23T20:59:14Z", "created_by": "dogfood-boardctl-run25", "acceptance_criteria": "1) `umbrella --skip-bad-lines` exists and degrades: every parseable row of every healthy child board is counted, each skipped board/line is reported with file:line on stderr, exit 1. 2) On the boardctl+warpfs pair above, `umbrella --stats` and `umbrella --list` print both boards' totals plus a SKIPPED block instead of aborting. 3) Without the flag the current fail-closed behaviour is unchanged (rc=1, same message). 4) `umbrella --help` documents both modes, and a regression test drives a fixture umbrella whose second child carries a duplicate-key line. 5) `go test ./...` exits 0.", "capability_tags": [], "complexity": 3, "depen