 {"id": "DF-BOARDCTL-50", "title": "no boardctl verb can set row acceptance_criteria — the fleet's dispatchability requirement forces every agent to hand-edit tasks.jsonl in raw JSON, bypassing the id/shape guards and the BT-050 lock", "status": "in_progress", "priority": "P2", "reasoning": "Dogfood run 25 (tick boardctl-dogfood-2026-10-23-10-52-34), second delivery. Found while filing this run's own rows: the fleet's foremen will not dispatch a row without acceptance_criteria, but there is no flag to write it.\n\nEVIDENCE: `boardctl create --id TEST-AA-1 --title t --acceptance-criteria 'must do x'` -> rc=1, 'flag provided but not defined: -acceptance-criteria'. `boardctl update --help` has no acceptance flag either (34 flags listed, none named acceptance). README mentions acceptance_criteria only as a DRIFT KEY the normalize-board repair rewrites (README:476, 811, 823) — the tool can repair that key but cannot author it. This run's rows and the sibling delivery's DF-BOARDCTL-44..47 all had their criteria appended 'line-wise' by a python JSONL edit, i.e. exactly the bypass README:1262-1264 warns about ('Appending rows with your own JSON serialization bypasses the id-refusal and shape guards AND this lock — that bypass is the known source of duplicate-id corruption on fleet boards').\n\nConsequence: the sanctioned workflow has no sanctioned path for a required field, so every lane takes the unsanctioned one; the resulting interleave is exactly what produced the duplicate-id corruption BT-050 was written to stop. Secondary: the same gap exists for other foreman-consumed fields (e.g. capability_tags is settable at create, acceptance is not), so a row can be created dispatchable-looking but undispatched.", "created_at": "2026-10-23T11:26:21Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-23T13:02:35Z", "created_by": null, "acceptance_criteria": "1) A dispatchable row must be authorable through the locked write path: `boardctl create --id TEST-AA-1 --title t` plus the new acceptance flag must exit 0 and print 'created task TEST-AA-1'; `boardctl update --id TEST-AA-1` with that same flag must exit 0 and print the updated row with the criteria present in .coding-hermes/board/tasks.jsonl under acceptance_criteria. 2) `boardctl create --help` and `boardctl update --help` must both print a line for that flag (grep their output for 'acceptance' and expect 1 or more matches) and README.md's create/update usage block documents it, so the dispatchability note stops implying a hand edit. 3) A test creates a row with multi-line criteria and reads it back byte-exact including newlines: `go test ./internal/board -run Write` expected exit code 0. 4) With the flag absent, no empty-string acceptance_criteria key is written: `grep -c acceptance_criteria` of the created line prints 0, and `boardctl validate` still prints RESULT: OK with the missing field as a warning, not an error (exit 0). 5) Full suite exits 0: `go test ./...` expected exit code 0.", "capability_tags": [], "complexity": 3, "depends_on": [], "foreman_note": null, "commit_hash": null, "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "worker_summary": "Wave dispatch staged; worker running.", "detail": {"fingerprint": "5c88fe7eff9792b87827a96a410c88ba69ceda88f2b96c97cfa69c92444d12ab", "evidence": [{"run_id": "boardctl-dogfood-2026-10-23-10-52-34", "ts": "2026-10-23T11:26:21Z"}]}, "worker_status": "in_progress", "worktree": "/home/kara/worktrees/coding-hermes-boardctl-DF-BOARDCTL-50", "branch": "wt/DF-BOARDCTL-50"}
